{"name":"Buddy Buddy","hex":"#976538","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buddy buddy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of buddy-buddy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buddy_buddy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buddy Buddy","blocks":[{"text":"Buddy Buddy is a 1981 American comedy film based on Francis Veber's play Le contrat and Édouard Molinaro's film L'emmerdeur. It is the final film directed and written by Billy Wilder."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5e/Buddy_buddy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddy_Buddy"},{"title":"Buddy (2026 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Buddy is a 2026 American postmodernist supernatural black comedy slasher film directed by Casper Kelly and written by Kelly and Jamie King. The film stars Cristin Milioti, Delaney Quinn, Patton Oswalt, Clint Howard, Michael Shannon, Topher Grace, and Keegan-Michael Key as the voice of the title character. The film follows children trapped inside a surreal 1990s Barney & Friends-style children's television series who must find a way to escape their malevolent unicorn television host."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Buddy_%282026_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddy_(2026_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Keegan-Michael_Key_%2849550965587%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Keegan-Michael_Key_%2849550965587%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Keegan-Michael_Key_%2849550965587%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Keegan-Michael_Key_%2849550965587%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.w